# ip-bar configuration
#
# Copy this file to ".env" in the same folder and edit the values you need.
# EVERY setting is optional — with no .env at all the widget runs fine using
# the defaults shown below. Nothing here is a secret: these are file paths and
# hostnames. The widget never asks you for an API key.
#
#   copy .env.example .env
#
# Restart the widget after editing (see README "Restarting").


# ── AI usage panel ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The widget reads the OAuth token that the Claude Code and Codex CLIs already
# wrote when you logged in. It never sees your password and never stores a
# token itself. If you do not use these CLIs, leave this section alone — the
# AI rows will simply say "setup" and everything else keeps working.
#
# By default it looks in your Windows user profile:
#     %USERPROFILE%\.claude\.credentials.json
#     %USERPROFILE%\.codex\auth.json
#
# If you run the CLIs inside WSL, the tokens live in your Linux home instead.
# Point the widget at them here. Separate multiple paths with ";" — the first
# readable one wins, so you can list a WSL path and a Windows path together.
#
# Replace "Ubuntu" with your distro name and "youruser" with your Linux user:

#CLAUDE_CRED_PATHS=\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\home\youruser\.claude\.credentials.json
#CODEX_CRED_PATHS=\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\home\youruser\.codex\auth.json

# Both CLIs, listing WSL first and falling back to Windows:
#CLAUDE_CRED_PATHS=\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\home\youruser\.claude\.credentials.json;C:\Users\You\.claude\.credentials.json


# ── Ping targets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The two hosts shown in the LATENCY row. Defaults are Cloudflare and Google
# DNS. Point them at your gateway or a work server if that is more useful.

#PING_HOST_1=1.1.1.1
#PING_HOST_2=8.8.8.8


# ── Log file ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the widget appends its log. Default is ip_bar_log.txt in your home
# folder. "Open Log" in the right-click menu opens whatever this points at.

#LOG_FILE=%USERPROFILE%\ip_bar_log.txt
